# Trivy misconfiguration findings that are deliberate in this repo.
# Each entry states why. An unexplained entry is not acceptable --
# see CONTRIBUTING.md.

# AVD-AWS-0104: Security group allows egress to multiple public
# destinations.
#
# The access node's egress is the variable egress_cidr_blocks, which
# defaults to 0.0.0.0/0 because an access node that cannot reach your
# datastores serves no purpose, and hardcoding a guess at your database
# port would break more deployments than it protected. There is NO
# corresponding ingress rule and no way to create one -- the module has
# no ingress resource and no variable for it. The private-subnets
# example narrows egress to the VPC CIDR, which is the documented
# recommendation.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AVD-AWS-0057: IAM policy with wildcard resource.
#
# Three places, all unavoidable and each commented in the source:
#   * the five Session Manager ssmmessages actions operate on the
#     agent's own control/data channel, which has no ARN to name --
#     this matches AWS's documented minimal instance policy
#   * ssm:DescribeInstanceInformation has no resource-level permission
#     support at all
#   * ec2:DescribeInstances and ssm:DescribeSessions are list
#     operations that accept no resource ARN
# All are read-only or channel-scoped. Access is constrained by the
# ssm:resourceTag condition on StartSession, which is the control that
# actually matters.
AVD-AWS-0057

# AVD-AWS-0017: CloudWatch log group is not encrypted.
#
# False positive against the module's conditional resource: the log
# group sets kms_key_id unconditionally from local.kms_key_arn, and
# terraform test asserts it. Trivy cannot resolve the local through the
# count expression.
AVD-AWS-0017
